//! CII prohibitions, extracted from CEN's preprocessed Schematron.
//!
//! **Generated by `cargo xtask codegen`. Do not edit.**
//!
//! # Each prohibition is context-relative, and the context is the point
//!
//! `CII-…` rules of the form `not(x)` do **not** say "no document may
//! contain `x`". They say "the element this rule's context selects may not
//! have an `x` child". An earlier version of this table dropped the context
//! and turned narrow prohibitions into blanket ones — which made the writer
//! discard `ram:ID` everywhere. So each entry carries
//! `(rule, context, relative path)`, and a match requires both halves.
//!
//! Source is the **preprocessed** artefact, where `<rule context="…">` is a
//! fully resolved XPath rather than a `$Variable` reference.
//!
//! 447 element and 0 attribute prohibitions are represented.
//! [`UNEXTRACTED`] = 75 are not: their context is conditional (a
//! predicate, `ends-with(…)`, a wildcard) and selecting the elements it
//! matches needs an XPath engine this crate does not have. That number is
//! public so a test reports "447 of 522 checked" rather than
//! implying a clean sweep.

